@*
    The voice that narrates an empire's game.

    A tab of its own in the game's editor, and short enough here to be one panel rather than a corner
    of another. The game frames it as a choice between letting the empire pick a voice for itself and
    naming one; a design that names none is the first of those, which is what an empty selection means
    here.
*@

<div class="sem-options">
    @*
        The first of the game's two modes, and for a long time the one no control could reach: every
        card wrote a voice and nothing wrote none, so an empire that had been left to choose for
        itself could not be put back that way once anything was clicked. The game's own wording, and
        the same answer the room picker's None tile gives - a design may name nothing, and there has
        to be a way back to naming nothing.
    *@
    <OptionCard Name="@Session.Localizer.Text("SETTINGS_VOICE_TYPE_auto_advisor_voice_type", "Based on Government")"
                Description="@Session.Localizer.Text("SETTINGS_VOICE_TYPE_auto_advisor_voice_type_DESC", string.Empty)"
                Selected="@string.IsNullOrEmpty(Design.AdvisorVoiceType)"
                OnSelect="() => Session.Edit(d => d.AdvisorVoiceType = null)" />

    @foreach (var voice in Voices)
    {
        <OptionCard Name="@Session.Localizer.Text(voice.NameKey, Localizer.Prettify(voice.Key))"
                    Icon="@voice.Icon"
                    Selected="@(voice.Key == Design.AdvisorVoiceType)"
                    OnSelect="() => Session.Edit(d => d.AdvisorVoiceType = voice.Key)" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }

    private EmpireDesign Design => Session.Current!;

    private IEnumerable<AdvisorVoiceDefinition> Voices => Session.Data.Database.AdvisorVoices;
}
